#quote-box[
#set text(fill: black)
Let $P(s)$ and $C(s)$ denote the plant and controller transfer functions respectively. 
 
 a) Draw the block diagram of the closed-loop system. Your diagram should include the following signals:
  -   the reference $r(t)$,
  -   the controlled input $u(t)$,
  -   the controlled output $y(t)$,
  -   the load disturbance $d(t)$,
  -   the output noise $n(t)$.
]
The standard feedback block diagram is shown in @fig-blockdiagram. The controller
$C(s)$ processes the tracking error $e(t) = r(t) - y(t)$ to generate the
control input $u(t)$. The load disturbance $d(t)$ enters at the plant input,
while the measurement noise $n(t)$ corrupts the output before it reaches the
feedback path.
